# Frontend Patterns

> For full detail see `FRONTEND_STRUCTURE.md`. This rule captures the constraints agents most commonly get wrong.

## Structure

```
frontend/src/
  pages/          # One file per route/page
  components/     # Shared reusable components
  contexts/       # AuthContext.jsx, OrgContext.jsx (+ OrgContext.test.js), SyncContext.jsx
  services/       # api.js — single Axios instance
  locales/        # en.json, sr.json
  i18n/           # index.js — language registration
  styles.css      # Global styles
```

## Auth & RBAC

- JWT stored in `localStorage` after login. Axios interceptor in `api.js` adds `Authorization: Bearer <token>`.
- Wrap protected pages with `ProtectedRoute`. Wrap action-gated sections with `ActionProtectedRoute` (uses action code, not role name).
- Show/hide actions and sensitive fields based on role action codes. Never branch on role name strings in UI logic.
- Respect active client/organization scope — hide or disable actions outside the user's org access.
- **Global active org:** Operational pages read `activeOrgId` / `activeOrg` from `useOrg()` ([`OrgContext.jsx`](frontend/src/contexts/OrgContext.jsx)). The topbar [`OrganizationSwitcher`](frontend/src/components/AppShell.jsx) is the single org picker for migrated pages; do not add per-page org dropdowns unless the page manages a different scope (e.g. admin assignment forms, ApiConfig connection create, Email Templates modal).
- **No-org hint:** One banner per page — `<p className="muted org-scope-hint">` with `orgSwitcher.selectPrompt`. No duplicate inner empty-state org prompts.
- **Org load error:** `OrgContext.error === 'loadFailed'` is surfaced in the header switcher via `orgSwitcher.loadFailed` (not the "no organizations" pill).
- **OrgContext role check:** Use `isSuperAdmin(user)` from [`permissions.js`](frontend/src/utils/permissions.js) to choose `orgsApi.list()` vs `myAccess()` — do not inline `roleName === 'SUPERADMIN'` in new code.
- Self-deletion: always disable or hide the delete action for the currently logged-in user.

## API Client

- All API calls go through the centralized Axios instance in `services/api.js`. Do not create separate `fetch` or Axios instances except for SSE streams (use `fetch` + `ReadableStream` with Bearer token in header for SSE — `EventSource` does not support custom headers).
- Base URL proxied via Vite in development (`/api`).
- Global handlers: `401` → redirect to login, `403` → show access denied.

## UI Patterns

Apply these patterns consistently across all pages — see `FRONTEND_STRUCTURE.md` §3 for full specs:

- **App Shell:** Header (top) + collapsible sidebar (left) + main content area. Header and sidebar are separate reusable components included on every authenticated page.
- **List Workspace:** Fetch Filters → Actions Bar → Table → Pagination. Use for Orders, Fiscal Bills, Products, Users.
- **Two-Phase Filtering:** Phase 1 = server-side fetch filters; Phase 2 = client-side narrowing on loaded data.
- **Summary-to-Detail:** Grouped summary rows first; expand or open detail pane for line-level data.
- **Bulk Action:** Select rows → select action → confirmation modal with affected count → execute → show result summary.
- **Status Chip:** Consistent color + label chip across all modules. Same status always uses the same chip style.
- **State Feedback:** Every async view must handle all three states explicitly: loading (skeleton/spinner), empty (explain why + next action), error (clear message + retry + reference ID if available).
- **Role Deletion:** Confirmation modal always opens. Include optional reassignment selector. Show `409` inline in modal if role is in use and no reassignment is chosen. Block built-in system roles client-side before sending a request.
- **Table row actions:** Wrap Edit/Delete buttons in `.table-row-actions` inside the `<td>`. Destructive row actions use `.secondary-button.danger`; modal confirm buttons use `.primary-button.danger`.

## Internationalization

**Never hardcode user-visible text in JSX.** This includes labels, placeholders, `title`, `alt`, and `aria-label`.

- Use `useTranslation()` + `t('key')` in components; `i18next.t()` in non-React code (e.g. `AuthContext`).
- Catalogs: `frontend/src/locales/en.json` and `sr.json`. Key sets must be identical across both files (same keys, same `{{placeholder}}` names).
- Any label/message change must update both locale files in the same change.
- **Serbian plurals:** English uses `*_one` / `*_other`. Serbian adds `*_few` for Slavic plural rules (2–4). Define all three suffixes in `sr.json` when adding new counted strings.
- **RBAC display names:** Translate via `roles.actionLabels`, `roles.permissionDescriptions`, `roles.permissionModules` keyed by `actionCode`. Never translate the action code itself.
- **Icon-only controls:** Keep the glyph but provide a localized `aria-label` (e.g. `common.close`) in every supported language.
- **Do not translate:** `className`, `id`, API paths, enum/code `value` attributes, object keys, `console` output, MerchantPro/Tax API field names.
- **Lint:** Run `npm run lint` in `frontend/` before finishing. `eslint-plugin-i18next` flags hardcoded text in JSX, `title`, `placeholder`, `aria-label`, and `alt` attributes.
- **After large English catalog changes:** run `node frontend/scripts/build-sr-locale.mjs` to regenerate `sr.json`, then hand-edit domain-specific Serbian strings as needed.
